        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw9gaoxq-fdhdlh",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Depart at 08:00.\n\nToday you’ll visit Chagres National Park and Tusipono, a village of the Emberá people. Learn about the pre-Columbian history of Panama and Mesoamerica, the origins of the Emberá, and their traditions, crafts and daily life.\n\nLocal artisans make intricately woven baskets, sculptures from reddish cocobolo wood, tagua nut figurines, necklaces and bracelets. You’ll see traditional dances and can join in.\n\nA highlight of the day is a ride along the Chagres River in a traditional dugout canoe. Continue to Chorro del Mono waterfall, where you can swim. Capuchin and howler monkeys sometimes come down to the waterfall.\n\nA traditional Emberá lunch will be served in the village, with fried tilapia, fried bananas and fruit.\n\nWear lace-up athletic shoes with a closed heel that can get wet. Depending on the season, reaching the waterfall involves walking along a jungle trail and wading across a stream. The water can be knee-deep."
    },
